From 5ec203b7fe46a9cba5445ca3013f1074099d45d8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Jonathan D.A. Jewell" <6759885+hyperpolymath@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 10:05:27 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] ci: gate patch coverage, measure sensitivity, add the
 estate lanes
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The coverage report on this pull request said "52.38095% with 30 lines missing"
and nothing failed: patch coverage was `informational: true`, so an unreachable
adapter was a number in a comment rather than a problem with a pull request to
fix it in. It is a gate now, at 90%, with no tolerance, `precision: 2` and
`round: down` so a report cannot round its way past the bar. The project status
also stops comparing a fraction measured on a run whose tests failed.

Coverage counts lines that ran. Three additions count other things:

- `test/unit/test_differential_sensitivity.jl` measures whether the differential
  methods find a signal that is known to be there: a negative-binomial community
  with eight taxa multiplied fourfold, eight divided and eight unchanged, scored
  after BH at 0.05 for sensitivity, specificity and precision, against a
  label-permuted control. Every other test in the suite compares a method with a
  reference implementation of the same method, which a method that calls
  everything significant would also pass; the control is what that cannot pass.
  Floors are loose on purpose (0.625/0.625/0.6) and the metrics are themselves
  unit-tested against a table scored by hand, so a broken counter cannot produce
  a passing report.
- `scripts/ci/check-sensitivity-evidence.jl` reads the measurement and decides
  whether it is evidence: a missing file is a failure (a skipped measurement is
  not a pass), a value below its floor is a failure, a `passed` flag the numbers
  contradict is a failure, and an `Actually-Proven` tier is a failure because
  this lane cannot produce one. Each claim is Provisionally-Proven in the sense
  of hyperpolymath/proven-tests-and-benches: derived from a test that ran, never
  declared. The CI step writes the table to the job summary and keeps the JSON
  as an artifact.
- `scripts/ci/mutants-differential.sh` asks whether the suite would NOTICE: ten
  deliberate corruptions of the native adapter (BH applied twice, the wrong
  column as the estimate, log10 for log2, structural decisions ignored, the
  contrast direction swapped, the seam bypassed, the one-taxon floor removed,
  the composition refusal swallowed, the package name hardcoded, a NaN
  published) run against the focused suite. The unmutated baseline runs first; a
  survivor fails the step; a mutant that dies of a syntax error fails it too.
  Adapted from scripts/mutants.sh and scripts/julia-mutants.sh in
  hyperpolymath/MetaManifold-Evidence. None needs R, because the stand-in
  backend is what runs.

Then the estate lanes, each calling the shared canon at a commit where the
reusable exists (checked against the API, not assumed) instead of copying it:

- `.github/workflows/hypatia-scan.yml` — the neurosymbolic governance scan, with
  the pons-asinorum (`pons-ref`) and panic-attack (`panic-ref`, the scanner
  behind the fleet's panicbot) rows pinned explicitly so the checker cannot move
  without a commit here. It reports rather than blocks for now: `block-on-high`
  becomes the change that triages the first run's findings into a baseline or a
  named exemption, because gating before that would fail pull requests for
  findings that predate them.
- `.github/workflows/k9-deed-conformance.yml` — DEED and K9 conformance. This
  repository carries neither yet, so `require-files` is false and an empty
  corpus is grey rather than red; the change that adds the deed and the
  contracts flips it.
- `.github/workflows/cicd-squabbler.yml` — `squabble chains` as a hard gate
  (cycles and dead upstreams fail, and so does a tool that cannot look), with the
  fight report left advisory and not run without a credential that can read
  classic branch protection.

None of the three renames or replaces a required check; `Julia tests`,
`Agda proofs` and `REUSE compliance` keep their names and their matrix-free
shapes, and `test/unit/test_install_pins.jl` keeps enforcing that for `ci.yml`.
`docs/guide/development.md` gains a "Continuous verification" section stating
what each gate measures, what it explicitly does not claim, and how to run it
locally.

