+# SPDX-FileCopyrightText: 2026 Joshua Benjamin Jewell
+# SPDX-FileCopyrightText: 2026 Jonathan D.A. Jewell (hyperpolymath) <j.d.a.jewell@open.ac.uk>
+# SPDX-License-Identifier: MPL-2.0
+
+## Hypatia estate security scan
+#
+# The estate's neurosymbolic CI/CD governance scanner, run as a caller of the
+# shared reusable rather than copied: every rule, baseline and severity decision
+# then arrives from the canon at one pinned commit instead of drifting here.
+#
+# WHAT THE GRID CARRIES, AND THE TWO NAMES IN IT
+# ----------------------------------------------
+# Hypatia's verdict grid gives one row per tool. Two of those rows are the ones
+# this repository cares about most, because both read the Julia and Python
+# analysis code rather than only the workflow files:
+#
+#   * ponsbot — hyperpolymath/pons-asinorum, the depth-first scanner for wasted
+#     work, self-contradiction and missing escape hatches. It is passed as
+#     `pons-ref`.
+#   * panicbot — hyperpolymath/panic-attack, universal stress testing and
+#     logic-based bug signatures (the gitbot-fleet adapter in
+#     bots/panicbot/ wraps the same scanner). It is passed as `panic-ref`.
+#
+# All three refs are passed EXPLICITLY even though the reusable declares the
+# same values as defaults at the commit pinned below. Two reasons, both
+# measured elsewhere in this estate rather than guessed: a lane that silently
+# follows the reusable's moving default changes its checker when nobody is
+# looking at this repository, and a scan whose tool versions are not in the
+# caller's diff cannot be reviewed. The values below are the reusable's declared
+# defaults at `9bdf864c`, so this changes nothing about today's behaviour and
+# everything about tomorrow's. When the estate moves a default, that move must
+# arrive here as a commit.
+#
+# WHAT THIS LANE DOES NOT DO
+# --------------------------
+# It does not change the required-check contract. The required contexts
+# (`Julia tests`, `Agda proofs`, `REUSE compliance`) keep their names and their
+# matrix-free shapes; `test/unit/test_install_pins.jl` enforces that for
+# `ci.yml`, and this file leaves `ci.yml` alone. A failing row here is a finding
+# to triage against `.hypatia-baseline.json` or an exemption in
+# `.hypatia-exemptions.adoc`, not a licence to edit the required set.
+#
+# The scan is expensive (it builds three scanners). It runs on main, on every
+# pull request, weekly, and on demand; it is not attached to a path filter,
+# because a path-filtered security lane never reports on the changes that miss
+# the filter.
+
+name: Hypatia Security Scan
+
+on:
+  push:
+    branches: [main]
+  pull_request:
+  schedule:
+    - cron: "47 5 * * 1"
+  workflow_dispatch:
+
+permissions:
+  actions: read
+  contents: read
+  security-events: write
+
+concurrency:
+  group: ${{ github.workflow }}-${{ github.ref }}
+  cancel-in-progress: true
+
+jobs:
+  hypatia:
+    name: Hypatia neurosymbolic scan
+    uses: hyperpolymath/standards/.github/workflows/hypatia-scan-reusable.yml@9bdf864cc7f2c8e24b4df84bf00d04158eee3ad5
+    # Only the one secret the callee declares. `secrets: inherit` would forward
+    # every repository secret to a workflow that asked for one of them
+    # (standards#1108 §6b), and the estate's linter refuses it.
+    secrets:
+      HYPATIA_SCAN_PAT: ${{ secrets.HYPATIA_SCAN_PAT }}
+    with:
+      hypatia-ref: adb2f41db34156cf81b2508f6596a10c7f076098
+      pons-ref: bca1ea289a4f8a86bac6212731e6f8ec15c67ad4
+      panic-ref: 410a8f821ea8297833162565b50a298f787815da
+      # Reporting, not gating, for the first runs. A scan whose findings cannot
+      # fail anything is a dashboard, and that is why this is temporary: the
+      # first run's findings have to be triaged into `.hypatia-baseline.json` or
+      # named in `.hypatia-exemptions.adoc` before they can be a gate. Flipping
+      # this to true is the commit that makes them one, and it should be a commit
+      # whose diff is the triage itself — turning it on before that would fail
+      # this repository's pull requests for findings that predate them, which is
+      # the failure mode that got a validator deleted instead of the findings
+      # fixed elsewhere in this estate.
+      block-on-high: false
+      # Below-threshold findings stay out of the JSON too: nothing consumes them
+      # yet, and a report nobody reads is not worth the artefact.
+      hypatia-advisory: false
