+## Continuous verification
+
+CI is three required checks — `Julia tests`, `Agda proofs`, `REUSE compliance` — and a set of
+lanes beside them. The names of the required checks are load-bearing: a branch ruleset
+matches a required status check by the display name GitHub posts, and a check that is renamed
+or that embeds a matrix combination is simply absent, which no pull request can satisfy.
+`test/unit/test_install_pins.jl` asserts over every job in `ci.yml` that the name interpolates
+nothing and that the job has no matrix, so the rule cannot regress silently. Nothing below
+renames or replaces those three.
+
+### Coverage
+
+Julia line coverage of `src/` is uploaded to Codecov by the test job; the TypeScript frontend
+is not measured through that report, and `codecov.yml` says so rather than letting a
+frontend-sized blind spot read as a guarantee.
+
+Patch coverage is a gate at 90%, with no tolerance. It used to be informational, and the cost
+of that was measurable: the native `aldex2`/`ancombc` adapter in `src/analysis/differential.jl`
+landed at 38.77% patch coverage, because the estimators need `CompositionalDA`, which is not in
+the General registry, so no checkout CI can produce has it and the adapter's whole body was
+unreachable there. An informational setting meant that reason never had to be stated.
+
+The fix was a seam rather than a lower bar: `differential_abundance(...; native_backend=…)`
+calls a module instead of the package name, so `test/support/native_da_stub.jl` can supply a
+stand-in with the same entry points, columns and verdict strings, and
+`test/unit/test_differential_native.jl` exercises the production path with it. The result
+records which module produced it under `diagnostics.native_method.package`, so a record made
+with the stand-in cannot be read as one made with the package.
+
+### Sensitivity, specificity and precision
+
+Every other test in the suite asks whether a method computes what it says it computes. None can
+tell a working method from one that calls every taxon significant, because such a method is
+consistent with its own reference implementation. `test/unit/test_differential_sensitivity.jl`
+is the external check: a negative-binomial community is simulated with a known answer (eight
+taxa multiplied fourfold in the contrast condition, eight divided, eight unchanged), the real
+analyses are run on it, and the calls are scored after Benjamini-Hochberg at 0.05.
+
+```
+sensitivity = tp / (tp + fn)    of the taxa that really differ, how many were called
+specificity = tn / (tn + fp)    of the taxa that do not, how many were left alone
+precision   = tp / (tp + fp)    the complement of the false discovery proportion
+```
+
+Two things keep it from being a tautology. A label-permuted control re-runs the same counts with
+the group labels shuffled, destroying every real difference; a method whose sensitivity survives
+that is measuring its own threshold, and that comparison — not the absolute floors, which are
+deliberately loose — is the strong assertion. The metric functions themselves are unit-tested
+against a table whose scores are known by hand, so a broken counter cannot produce a passing
+report.
+
+The measurement is written to `test/artifacts/differential-sensitivity.json` (ignored by git: a
+stale copy must not speak for a run that never happened) and read by
+`scripts/ci/check-sensitivity-evidence.jl`, which refuses the file when a claim has no measured
+value, when a value contradicts its floor, when `passed` is not what the numbers imply, or when
+the file is absent — a skipped measurement is not a pass. Each claim is graded
+`Provisionally-Proven` in the sense of `hyperpolymath/proven-tests-and-benches`: demonstrated by
+a test that ran and passed, never proved. The checker refuses an `Actually-Proven` claim, because
+this lane cannot produce one.
+
+```bash
+julia --project=. test/runtests.jl differential_sensitivity   # measure (needs R with MASS)
+julia --project=. scripts/ci/check-sensitivity-evidence.jl    # read the evidence
+```
+
+### Test sensitivity (mutants)
+
+Coverage counts lines that ran. `scripts/ci/mutants-differential.sh` counts lines that would be
+*noticed* if they were wrong: ten deliberate, plausible corruptions of the native adapter (BH
+applied twice, the wrong column published as the estimate, the contrast direction swapped, the
+seam bypassed, a non-finite statistic published) each run against a focused suite. The
+unmutated baseline runs first and must pass, because a survivor only means something against a
+green baseline. A mutant that survives fails the step: the suite does not constrain that
+behaviour. A mutant that dies of a syntax error fails it too, since that proves the parser works
+rather than the tests. None of them needs R, because the stand-in backend is what is exercised.
+
+```bash
+bash scripts/ci/mutants-differential.sh          # run every mutant
+bash scripts/ci/mutants-differential.sh --list   # the labels only
+```
+
+Adapted from `scripts/mutants.sh` and `scripts/julia-mutants.sh` in
+`hyperpolymath/MetaManifold-Evidence` (AGPL-3.0-or-later), which hold the same line for the Agda
+proofs and the grid certificate.
+
+### Estate lanes
+
+Three lanes call the shared canon (`hyperpolymath/standards`) instead of copying it, each pinned
+to a commit at which the reusable exists — checked against the API, not assumed. They add no
+required status check.
+
+| Workflow | What it does | What it does not do |
+|---|---|---|
+| `hypatia-scan.yml` | Runs the neurosymbolic governance scan. Its grid carries the pons-asinorum row (`pons-ref`) and the panic-attack row (`panic-ref`, the scanner behind the fleet's `panicbot`), both pinned explicitly so the checker cannot move without a commit here. | It reports rather than blocks for now: high findings become a gate in the change that triages the first run's findings into a baseline or a named exemption. Flipping `block-on-high` before that would fail pull requests for findings that predate them. |
+| `k9-deed-conformance.yml` | Lints the DEED repository deed and typechecks the K9 contracts from `.machine_readable/contractiles/`. | This repository carries neither yet, so `require-files` is false and an empty corpus is grey, not red. The change that adds the deed and the contracts flips it to true; a manifest written to satisfy a validator would defeat the lane. |
+| `cicd-squabbler.yml` | `squabble chains` maps reusable-workflow and action edges across repositories, so a dead upstream or a cycle is found while the board reads green. Exit 4 fails; exit 2 (the tool could not look) fails too. | The `fight-report` half is advisory and never passes `--apply`. Without a credential that can read classic branch protection it reports NOT RUN rather than guessing. |
+
+The first run of `hypatia-scan.yml` is the measurement that decides whether `block-on-high`
+can be flipped in the next pull request; nothing in this guide should be read as a promise
+about findings that have not been scanned yet.
+
